Z||000000||SibERThuG||10-15-2000||11:41 PM||||At first I thought I would go and put airbag suspension on my car, a very cool idea. The ability to ride stock height, lower, lower, lower, or at shows, put the frame on the ground(literally). This, however, can not be done on a fiero! After going through companies and companies I've come to find out this kind of suspension is made for lowrider import cars or mini-trucks. So, I went with hydraulics. This SUCKS!!!! Don't do this. I have the ability to lower my car by slamming it to the ground after putting the front end 6ft in the air. I am going to damage the car and I know it! The hydros are comming out tomorrow. The stock suspension is being put back on. I am going to buy a airbag setup for another vehicle and try to modify it. I'd rather ruin airbags that cost $1500 where as the hydros cost $4000 and my car is worth about $5-6000. Just some advice before you decide or think about doing this to your car. I will let you know about the bags.<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||13
